A||N||16||Monkeyman||Wierd tail light bulb||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||05:09 AM||||I tried to get my '86 coupe started today and the battery was dead.  After I recharged the battery (starts fine but runs strange), I noticed that the far outside tail light bulb was considerably dimmer than the rest (I have the lens out).  I replaced the bulb, but noticed no change.  The rest are fine and equally bright.  Everything was kosher before my battery went dead.  Any thoughts?||||reg||5
Z||000001||2FAST4U||12-31-1999||05:50 AM||||Take the bulb back out. use some emry cloth (or an emry board from wife) and clean the contacts and inside of the socket. If that does't help the look for a bad ground. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||06:08 AM||||It's a new bulb, but I'll try that.  Everything worked just fine until my battery went dead.  How could that cause a short?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-31-1999||08:11 AM||||A battery going dead would not cause a short BUT could it be the other way around???????||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||01:09 PM||||Possible and something I hadn't thought of, but I haven't had any problems with the bulb until the other day and I've had the car for a couple of months.  I did however (only because I'm stupid) leave the tail light lens off for a few days and it snowed during that time.  I didn't turn the lights on while they were wet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||12-31-1999||02:22 PM||||A dimmer than normal bulb is almost always an indicator of a weak ground. You might of just got a little moisture in the socket that caused a little corrosion. Clean the bulb and socket, plus all the contacts and see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill Osmer||12-31-1999||05:51 PM||||One of your last "symptoms" was that it snowed on your tail lights. Water and dirt/oil make for interesting conduction paths that will be of varying resistances (read shorts). Once you clean everything (also making sure the new bulb is in the socket with the corrrect polarity), you'll probably find all's OK. Otherwise, more than likely, the snow got to other areas that is providing the shorted path. Can you get the car in a heated garage to dry it out for few days??? (I live in Indiana, and I've had to deal with snow causing electrical gremlins, too)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||01-01-2000||04:36 AM||||I have got to be the absolute dumbest guy in the world! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Instead of putting an 1157 (double filament) bulb in, I used an 1156 (single filament) bulb by mistake!!!!!!!!  (Don't ask me how I ever got it in there and locked in.)  I had to break the bulb to get it out, but finally I did and replaced it with the correct one and it works fine now.  I can't believe I did that.  I'm usually so anal that I'll spend more time checking to make sure I have the right part than it takes to install it!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   Argh!  Where is my medicine?!?!??||||reg||1
Z||000008||2FAST4U||01-01-2000||04:50 AM||||Not to worry<P>You had what is commonly reffered to as a "Brain Fart"<BR>It is a temporary thing and can be easily blamed on the Y2K bug.<P>Boy, just at the stroke of 12:00 sombody in the neighborhood set off a big honking explosion. I immediatly thought "oh s**t" here comes that Y2K thing before I had time to reailize it was just a big friggin firecracker, atleast I hope it was.<BR>Monkeyman can I borrow some drugs, I need em bad!<P>HAPPY NEWYEAR EVERYONE<P>2FAST4U||||reg||1
